# Answer key: CBronte_Jane.txt
#
# Source: a circulating plain-text Jane Eyre. Note that it carries NO Project
# Gutenberg apparatus at all: no header, no licence, no sentinel markers. The
# text begins directly with the title.
#
# Marked by reading the opening and closing of the file. The boundary that
# matters is line 24, where CHAPTER I begins. Everything before it is the
# author's front matter: title, byline, the 1847 preface and the 1848 note to
# the third edition, each ending with the "CURRER BELL" signature and a date.

1-2      front_matter   Title and byline
3-18     front_matter   PREFACE, ending "December 21st, 1847."
19-23    front_matter   NOTE TO THE THIRD EDITION, ending "April 13th, 1848."
24-4083  body           CHAPTER I through the end of CHAPTER XXXVIII
